$$
\begin{aligned}\int \sqrt[4]{x}-{x}^{5}\,\text{d}x & =\int {x}^{1/4}\,\text{d}x-\int {x}^{5}\,\text{d}x \\  & =\frac{{x}^{1/4+1}}{(\frac{1}{4}+1)}-\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{(5+1)}+C \\  & =\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{\left(\frac{5}{4}\right)}-\frac{{x}^{6}}{(6)}+C \\  & =\frac{4\sqrt[4]{{x}^{5}}}{5}-\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186234302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80a672a5-9018-5a78-9672-cf47be4d95f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{\sqrt{x}}+3x+C" :db/id 17592186566608} {:answer/id #uuid "98e55f7b-e970-5ec1-8f87-371c4a6f55f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{1}{\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}-4x+C" :db/id 17592186566663} {:answer/id #uuid "d87f3a3b-f1ff-5e22-81b2-679daf615e23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{\sqrt{x}}-x+C" :db/id 17592186566796} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4e8d2e-8e7f-55f8-887c-4c3c6d134e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\sqrt{x}+4x+C" :db/id 17592186566840} {:answer/id #uuid "f5261de7-027d-545e-bff9-4ea8c302891e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\frac{2}{\sqrt{x}}+4x+C" :db/id 17592186566855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5261de7-027d-545e-bff9-4ea8c302891e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\frac{2}{\sqrt{x}}+4x+C" :db/id 17592186566855} :answer-field/id #uuid "f689fbb7-4820-549d-86af-2dc10f9a0677" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186567001}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79aa6724-ce36-5977-907b-506fab54c4d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71169" :question/problem "Find the integral of $\frac{1}{\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+4.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:

$$
\begin{aligned}\int \frac{1}{\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+4\,\text{d}x & =\int \frac{1}{{x}^{3/2}}\,\text{d}x+4\int 1\,\text{d}x \\  & =\int {x}^{-3/2}\text{d}x+4\int {x}^{0}\text{d}x \\  & =\frac{{x}^{-3/2+1}}{(-\frac{3}{2}+1)}+4\left(\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1}\right)+C \\  & =-2\cdot {x}^{-1/2}+4x+C \\  & =-\frac{2}{\sqrt{x}}+4x+C\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186234303 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09d58888-0116-53f3-b47a-9d0d7153229f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71173" :question/problem "$\int 2+\frac{1}{{y}^{5}}\,\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:

$$
\begin{aligned}\int 2+\frac{1}{{y}^{5}}\,\text{d}y & =2\int 1\,\text{d}y+\int {y}^{-5}\,\text{d}y \\  & =2\int {y}^{0}\,\text{d}y+\int {y}^{-5}\,\text{d}y \\  & =2\left(\frac{{y}^{0+1}}{0+1}\right)+\frac{{y}^{-5+1}}{-5+1}+C \\  & =2y+\frac{{y}^{-4}}{-4}+C \\  & =2y-\frac{1}{4{y}^{4}}+C\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186541108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c412eada-9cf7-59a5-905e-0f6c0063eb13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{t^3}{3}-2t" :db/id 17592186540856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c412eada-9cf7-59a5-905e-0f6c0063eb13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{t^3}{3}-2t" :db/id 17592186540856} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1f591a2-abaf-568b-95d2-b28ddb7d4b0c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186541017}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "836e24be-b58e-500b-bb05-e9b2030ce5e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-133291" :question/problem "Find $y(t),$ the antiderivative of ${y}^{′}(t).$

$y(t)=$
