$+\,C$" :question/worked-solution "We know that ${y}^{′}(t)={t}^{2}-2.$

Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:

$$
\begin{aligned}\int {t}^{2}-2\,\text{d}t & =\int {t}^{2}\,\text{d}t-\int 2\,\text{d}t \\  & =\int {t}^{2}\,\text{d}t-2\int {t}^{0}\,\text{d}t \\  & =\left(\frac{{t}^{2+1}}{2+1}\right)-2t+C \\  & =\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-2t+C.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186567064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67ebaae1-1b6f-54a0-9ee3-20ad6d94b297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-{x}^{4}+C" :db/id 17592186566561} {:answer/id #uuid "75869535-6c65-5fee-b563-b5239aaa4910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{2}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}+C" :db/id 17592186566587} {:answer/id #uuid "949d1af7-fd39-55bc-bf6f-81a0c846d362" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}+C" :db/id 17592186566654} {:answer/id #uuid "a1102e39-908b-5d4b-9cc6-16a7726229bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id 17592186566676} {:answer/id #uuid "e18db342-254e-56c4-b18d-3e730f819b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+\frac{2{x}^{4}}{3}+C" :db/id 17592186566817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1102e39-908b-5d4b-9cc6-16a7726229bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id 17592186566676} :answer-field/id #uuid "abc76652-94ff-55a2-98b8-14e731f2dc71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186566961}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e4827b1-c8af-5e0e-a92c-bab0c6f19c7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71167" :question/problem "$\int 5-{x}^{3}\,\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:

$$
\begin{aligned}\int 5-{x}^{3}\,\text{d}x & =5\int 1\,\text{d}x-\int {x}^{3}\,\text{d}x \\  & =5\int {x}^{0}\,\text{d}x-\int {x}^{3}\,\text{d}x \\  & =5\left(\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1}\right)-\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}+C \\  & =5x-\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C\end{aligned}
$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum Rule"}
